From c136f26432f9e38ae0b63ba3933b23e09116b135 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tamer Ahmed <tamerahmed@microsoft.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 16:48:10 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] zebra: count a local MAC delete with no kernel entry as done

In SONiC's FPM MAC sync mode, dplane_fpm_sonic installs a sync MAC (a
host the Ethernet Segment peer advertises) in the ASIC as a static entry
when zebra writes the MAC as static, and removes the entry when zebra
deletes the MAC. It sees zebra's MAC writes after the kernel has made
them.

When the kernel has no entry for the MAC, it answers zebra's delete with
ENOENT. zebra's dataplane (zebra_dplane.c) hands each request to its
providers in turn, the kernel first and then dplane_fpm_sonic, and
returns a request the kernel fails to zebra at once
(dplane_thread_loop()), so dplane_fpm_sonic never sees the delete: the
ASIC keeps the static entry, and every FPM reconnect installs it again.
zebra is the only writer of these kernel entries, but in this mode it
ignores the kernel's FDB messages for local ports, so it does not notice
when an entry is removed outside FRR, for instance by bridge fdb del.

zebra asked for the entry to be gone, and it is, so report such a delete
as done, as netlink_parse_error() already does for a route delete
answered with ENODEV or ESRCH. Remote MAC deletes still fail on ENOENT:
one request removes both the bridge entry and the VXLAN device entry,
and the kernel stops at the bridge entry's ENOENT, so the VXLAN device
entry may still be there.

Signed-off-by: Tamer Ahmed <tamerahmed@microsoft.com>
---
 zebra/kernel_netlink.c | 14 +++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/zebra/kernel_netlink.c b/zebra/kernel_netlink.c
index 55b0312f64..894f0c3219 100644
--- a/zebra/kernel_netlink.c
+++ b/zebra/kernel_netlink.c
@@ -1145,6 +1145,18 @@ int netlink_request(struct nlsock *nl, void *req)
 	return 0;
 }
 
+/* The entry is already gone, so later providers (e.g. FPM) must still see it. */
+static bool nl_local_mac_del_already_gone(struct zebra_dplane_ctx *ctx,
+					  struct nlmsghdr *h)
+{
+	struct nlmsgerr *err = (struct nlmsgerr *)NLMSG_DATA(h);
+
+	return err->error == -ENOENT &&
+	       dplane_ctx_get_op(ctx) == DPLANE_OP_MAC_DELETE &&
+	       !CHECK_FLAG(dplane_ctx_mac_get_update_flags(ctx),
+			   DPLANE_MAC_REMOTE);
+}
+
 static int nl_batch_read_resp(struct nl_batch *bth, struct nlsock *nl)
 {
 	struct nlmsghdr *h;
@@ -1266,7 +1278,7 @@ static int nl_batch_read_resp(struct nl_batch *bth, struct nlsock *nl)
 			int err = netlink_parse_error(nl, h, bth->zns->is_cmd,
 						      false);
 
-			if (err == -1)
+			if (err == -1 && !nl_local_mac_del_already_gone(ctx, h))
 				dplane_ctx_set_status(
 					ctx, ZEBRA_DPLANE_REQUEST_FAILURE);
 
